(2378326, 324143, 14476, '<td valign="top">This image tells a beautiful story.  You have some good comments and I can only add my appreciation for a fine interpretation of the flower and the Challenge.  ((''m one of your five "nines")<br/> <br/>Keep up the good work.<br/>Alice</td>', 'This image tells a beautiful story.  You have some good comments and I can only add my appreciation for a fine interpretation of the flower and the Challenge.  ((''m one of your five "nines") Keep up the good work.Alice', '2006-05-03 17:13:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(2378365, 326465, 14414, '<td valign="top">ITs a nice simple idea, and I didnt even notice the red/blue thing for ages*, but the stick used as the division is a bit..well, ..boring imho. I would like to see the same idea but with something more dynamic - I''m sure I''m seen a similar design (albeit achieved in PS) with a lizard, that was used for some logo or something. <br/> <br/>The scratches on the blue b/g detract, guess they could easily be removed outside of basic editing. The idea is simple and cool but needs something extra for that ''wow''<br/> <br/>Hope you''re feeling better anyway :)<br/> <br/>*Yes, its very much red to me, but then again, my monitor isn''t greatly calibrated itself</td>', 'ITs a nice simple idea, and I didnt even notice the red/blue thing for ages*, but the stick used as the division is a bit..well, ..boring imho. I would like to see the same idea but with something more dynamic - I''m sure I''m seen a similar design (albeit achieved in PS) with a lizard, that was used for some logo or something.  The scratches on the blue b/g detract, guess they could easily be removed outside of basic editing. The idea is simple and cool but needs something extra for that ''wow'' Hope you''re feeling better anyway :) *Yes, its very much red to me, but then again, my monitor isn''t greatly calibrated itself', '2006-05-03 17:20:51.000000', NULL, 0),
