(2383611, 323886, 47294, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by cushla:</b></div><hr/><i> Alway''s the Bridesmaid when are going to get another top 5 finish - "you must be getting frustrated, keep Trying mate - Maybe you should take up slot car racing as a hobby?"<br/> <br/>Oh thats right you''ve have tried that! Who put a stop to that hobby, I like to refer to these people as "Handbrakes" or "Maniacs" </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Real FUNNY!</td>', 'Originally posted by cushla: Alway''s the Bridesmaid when are going to get another top 5 finish - "you must be getting frustrated, keep Trying mate - Maybe you should take up slot car racing as a hobby?" Oh thats right you''ve have tried that! Who put a stop to that hobby, I like to refer to these people as "Handbrakes" or "Maniacs"   Real FUNNY!', '2006-05-04 23:25:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(2383845, 323929, 12253, '<td valign="top">This is beautiful!  Great work and very creative.  New fav for me!</td>', 'This is beautiful!  Great work and very creative.  New fav for me!', '2006-05-05 00:51:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(2383915, 324633, 29269, '<td valign="top">What a fine photo! Haven''t voted in this challenge, but I would have easily given this a 7 in the first pass at least. As someone already indicated, the gray road (that has no complementary gray shade readily visible) is taking away from the mainstream flower/water droplet/color setup photo and hence the low scores. The car in the photo is small enough not to offer any details for the observer to enjoy, yet large enough to spoil the photo by taking away the attention from the nice leading lines.<br/> <br/>Exposure and focus are dead on, I wish you waited (how long is the question) for all the cars to leave the frame. Deserted road would have inched you up some score-wise I think.<br/> <br/>Keep up the good work. Stay out of the box and the voters will come one day...</td>', 'What a fine photo! Haven''t voted in this challenge, but I would have easily given this a 7 in the first pass at least. As someone already indicated, the gray road (that has no complementary gray shade readily visible) is taking away from the mainstream flower/water droplet/color setup photo and hence the low scores. The car in the photo is small enough not to offer any details for the observer to enjoy, yet large enough to spoil the photo by taking away the attention from the nice leading lines. Exposure and focus are dead on, I wish you waited (how long is the question) for all the cars to leave the frame. Deserted road would have inched you up some score-wise I think. Keep up the good work. Stay out of the box and the voters will come one day...', '2006-05-05 01:20:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(2384286, 325889, 37858, '<td valign="top">Good strong colors here...although the yellowish area of the leaves is a bit washed out on my monitor, I suspect from saturation.  The composition is really helpful, too.  I like how the flower and the leaves interact...at first glance they almost seem to be spiraling upwards together.  The lines formed by the leaves and flowers give this photo a lot of abstract punch.</td>', 'Good strong colors here...although the yellowish area of the leaves is a bit washed out on my monitor, I suspect from saturation.  The composition is really helpful, too.  I like how the flower and the leaves interact...at first glance they almost seem to be spiraling upwards together.  The lines formed by the leaves and flowers give this photo a lot of abstract punch.', '2006-05-05 04:33:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(2384290, 326465, 37858, '<td valign="top">Good job.  Love the idea and the colors.  The vine/wood piece seems slightly out of focus (unless it''s my tired eyes that are not focusing).  Other than that, I really like this photo and would have scored it a 6 or 7.</td>', 'Good job.  Love the idea and the colors.  The vine/wood piece seems slightly out of focus (unless it''s my tired eyes that are not focusing).  Other than that, I really like this photo and would have scored it a 6 or 7.', '2006-05-05 04:36:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(2384295, 325631, 37858, '<td valign="top">Beautiful purples, but the complementary yellow color seems too washed out.  I haven''t read any other comments yet, but I suspect "focus" issues predominated.  This would have been better, I think, if the yellows were more obvious and the flowers were more sharply focused.  I like the composition.  Nice use of diagonals.</td>', 'Beautiful purples, but the complementary yellow color seems too washed out.  I haven''t read any other comments yet, but I suspect "focus" issues predominated.  This would have been better, I think, if the yellows were more obvious and the flowers were more sharply focused.  I like the composition.  Nice use of diagonals.', '2006-05-05 04:40:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(2384616, 323621, 24486, '<td valign="top">Right place, right time. Love the perspective. Great colours too. Lucky you had a reasonably clean window to shoot through too.<br/> <br/>Congratulations on a top 10 finish.</td>', 'Right place, right time. Love the perspective. Great colours too. Lucky you had a reasonably clean window to shoot through too. Congratulations on a top 10 finish.', '2006-05-05 08:20:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(2384630, 323886, 44751, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by cushla:</b></div><hr/><i> Alway''s the Bridesmaid when are YOU going to get another top 5 finish - "you must be getting frustrated, keep Trying mate - Maybe you should take up slot car racing as a hobby?"<br/> <br/>Oh thats right you''ve tried that! Who put a stop to that hobby anyway?, <br/> <br/>I like to refer to these people as "Handbrakes" or in your case "Maniacs" </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Cushla!!  I''m going to quote this to Xan, you know</td>', 'Originally posted by cushla: Alway''s the Bridesmaid when are YOU going to get another top 5 finish - "you must be getting frustrated, keep Trying mate - Maybe you should take up slot car racing as a hobby?" Oh thats right you''ve tried that! Who put a stop to that hobby anyway?,  I like to refer to these people as "Handbrakes" or in your case "Maniacs"   Cushla!!  I''m going to quote this to Xan, you know', '2006-05-05 08:29:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(2384952, 326198, 92, '<td valign="top">I''m thinking I need new ideas and a bit more talent. You deserve EVERY ribbon you''ve won so never feel sorry ! Congrats !!!!</td>', 'I''m thinking I need new ideas and a bit more talent. You deserve EVERY ribbon you''ve won so never feel sorry ! Congrats !!!!', '2006-05-05 11:47:57.000000', NULL, 0),
